# Next.js 14 Frontend

## Stack
- App Router (`app/`), Server Components by default; `'use client'` only when needed
- Tailwind for styling; Zustand for client global state
- Strict TypeScript — no `any`

## Components
```tsx
interface Props {
  ticker: string;
  score: number;
}

const ScoreBadge = ({ ticker, score }: Props) => (
  <span className="rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm font-medium text-slate-100 bg-emerald-600">
    {ticker}: {score}
  </span>
);
```

## Patterns
- Colocate types in `types/` or next to feature modules
- Data fetching: prefer Server Components + fetch; client mutations via Server Actions or API routes
- Zustand stores: narrow slices, avoid mirroring server state unnecessarily

## E2E
- Debug flows with Playwright MCP — snapshot a11y tree before claiming UI works

## Do not
- Mix Pages Router patterns into App Router without reason
- Ship components without typed props
- Rewrite whole pages for one-line fixes
